      "dom_id": "question-95567",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=-2\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\\,g=4x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=2{csch}^{2}\\,g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2{csch}^{2}⁡g\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8{csch}^{2}⁡g \\\\  & =8{csch}^{2}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
