      "dom_id": "question-95575",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=3{csch}^{2}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=3{g}^{2},\\,g=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=6g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =6g(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6{csch}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
