      "name": null,
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡x$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot {e}^{x}-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\cdot {({e}^{x})}^{′}}{{({e}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\cdot {e}^{x}-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\cdot ({e}^{x})}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}({csch}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{csch}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
