      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x}{2x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x$ and $v(x)=2x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x)}^{′}\\cdot 2x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x\\cdot {(2x)}^{′}}{{(2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2{csch}^{2}⁡2x)\\cdot 2x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x\\cdot (2)}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(2x{csch}^{2}⁡2x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x)}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x{csch}^{2}⁡2x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x}{2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
